From c26c9f23571827ac9ed683f3a6ae7709bd52cd7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: J P <jpwatters@mac.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 23:13:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/30] nas-kit: rebuild the NAS version from each new upstream
 release; PDF QMX-Panadapter-Shared

tools/nas-kit/make-qmx-panadapter-nas.sh clones SteffenLav/qmx-panadapter,
checks out its newest release tag and applies the six NAS commits
(tools/nas-kit/patches, git format-patch --binary v1.16.11..23342f6) with
git's 3-way merge into ~/src/QMX-Panadapter-NAS. --mark-tested copies a
hardware-tested NAS build to ~/src/QMX-Panadapter-Shared; replaced folders
are moved to ~/src/.qmx-panadapter-archive, never deleted. A patch that no
longer applies stops the run (exit 2) with NAS and Shared unchanged.

Tested: fresh run on v1.16.11 gives the tested tree exactly (ca6134e);
rerun, --force, --mark-tested, --status; upstream main applies cleanly;
a conflicting fake release stops at the right patch. Run on the Mac:
QMX-Panadapter-NAS and -Shared created.

QMX-Panadapter-Shared.pdf: the project document, now including the kit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W7MAsxunucnfwkhxdqp61S
